hi everyone it's me danny ceo and  welcome to do  just one thing  and you know that slogan put a cork in  it well how about 50  wine corks to make a really cool  upcycling project what we're going to  make today  is we're going to take your collection  of wine corks and make  a beautiful trivet for your kitchen and  you won't believe how simple  and easy it is it's actually a one step  craft project  even though it looks really beautiful  and complicated you don't need any  special tools you don't need any glues  or adhesive all you need  is a flathead screwdriver and maybe the  fun part is about  50 wine cork so i guess step one really  is drink a lot of vino this summer  and then save your wine corks the way  that this works is that we're going to  use something called  tension to keep everything in place and  this is the one investment you have to  make it comes in a lot of different  sizes  it's called a hose clamp it's a metal  hose clamp you find at the hardware  store it's in the plumbing section this  large one  cost about two dollars and they come in  smaller sizes you can make a small  coaster you can make a medium-sized  trivet or you can make an extra large  one like this one  and the way that it works is that all  the way on the side right here there's  like a flathead little screw right here  and then by twisting it it actually gets  tighter and tighter and tighter and  smaller and smaller  so the fun part is you take your wine  corks  and you simply place them all the way on  the  inside of the hose clamp and it's kind  of fun to do this because what you want  to do  is create a pattern and make sure there  aren't any gaps or any spaces in between  the corks  and you can do this with champagne corks  if you're going to a summer wedding  here's a fun idea why not save all of  the corks from the wedding and surprise  the married couple with a trivet that  she made using corks from the wedding if  you're one of those people where you're  like danny  how the heck am i going to drink 50  bottles of wine which  to me this seems reasonable but if  you're wondering how am i going to drink  50 bottles of wine my little inside  trick is  go to a local restaurant that maybe has  a wine bar  and bring a box or a bag and ask them  could you save the wine corks for me  so usually they're not saving them for  anything else and they'll happily save  them for you and you'll get  hundreds and hundreds of corks very  quickly and easily  so as you can see you want to fill the  entire thing up with wine corks i'm just  going to put these aside  to show you what the finished one looks  like here's the finished one  really really beautiful and if you find  that it's a little bit loose  you just take your flathead screwdriver  and you tighten it  and you can hear it like you can hear it  tightening around it  and it's all that tension that keeps  all these wine corks in place then you  put it on your kitchen countertop and  the next time you have a scorching hot  pan  just place it on top and it's completely  protected  one step project using wine corks do  just one thing  be sure to tag the drew barrymore show  in your instagram post and don't forget  to check out more projects at  thedrewberrymoreshow.com  and one more thing be sure to pick up  the newest issue of my magazine  naturally danny ceo  [Music]
 

